# Python Backend Standards

## Stack (locked)

- Python 3.14 · Litestar controllers · Pydantic v2 · `pydantic-settings`
- Outbound: process-scoped `httpx.AsyncClient` in lifespan (ADR 0002)
- Serve: Granian ASGI via `GRANIAN_*` image env — interface `asgi`, not `asginl`
- Logs: stdlib JSON via `onboarding_flow.logging_config`; `extra=` fields only
- Absolute imports only (`ban-relative-imports`)

## Seams to respect

- `UpstreamPort` on `app.state`; tests inject `MemoryUpstream` (or fakes) — never
  hit the real Encore URL in unit tests.
- `VehicleRequest` / `LicensePlate` at ingress; shared plate rules on success
  parse. Invalid ingress → 4xx (ADR 0001).
- Envelope: `APIResponse[T]` / `VehicleInfoResponse`; map `UpstreamOutcome` in
  `envelope.py`. Do not mint `trace_id` in handlers — read via observability.
- Settings: `UPSTREAM_URL`, `UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`, `LOG_LEVEL` only.

## Observability and PII

- `TraceMiddleware` accepts or replaces `X-Trace-ID`; ContextVar → every record.
- Five events only (see `ARCHITECTURE.md`). Never log raw plates, bodies, or
  PII; use `plate_mask`. Exception messages state the rule, never the value
  (`msg = "..."; raise X(msg)`); ruff `EM`/`TRY`/`G` enforce the shape, the
  500-path test enforces the content.
- Unhandled 5xx: `after_exception` → `request_failed`; 4xx stay silent.

## Verification

- Behavior changes: update unit tests at the public HTTP or port seam.
- Default gate: `./scripts/check.sh` (ruff, ty, `tests/unit`).
- Container smoke (optional): `./scripts/check-image.sh`.
